    "Card SFR (docs/refound/SFR_sim_fixture_coloured_phase_2026-10-01.md) re-base recipe, written by scripts/clock_level/sfr_calib.py recipe simnet60_quiet_col_24h --white 0.0005 --mp-phase 0.0 --pc-floor 20 --class tropical=0.006,300 --class mid=0.0049,300 --class high=0.0044,300.",
    "Identical to config/sim/simnet60_quiet_24h.json (commit 2306134) except the white phase noise, the multipath phase amplitude, the phase_colour block and the per-station phase_colour overrides by latitude class (tropical |lat| < 23.5, mid 23.5 to 50, high above 50 degrees), calibrated on the post-fit ionosphere-free phase residual of the field golden (scripts/clock_level/phase_acf.py).",
    "24 h QUIET stability fixture (2026-09-01): identical to simnet60_quiet_12h except the",
    "arc is anchored at 00:00:30 of DOY 129 (start_tow_s 302400 -> 259230, the first 30 s",
    "grid point strictly inside the day's IONEX map span [259218, 345618] GPS) and",
    "n_epochs 1440 -> 2879, so the FINAL epoch lands on tow 345570 = the 12 h fixture's",
    "exact trailing epoch (same product-day-edge tail condition as the validated bed; the",
    "leading 30 min sits in the 1800 s edge-margin WARNING zone = ignition).  Single product",
    "day throughout - a midnight-crossing arc would need multi-day SP3/CLK/GIM loading in",
    "BOTH the sim provider and the producer (a separate card).  Purpose: STABILITY target 1,",
    "settled-late-drift vs carry age over h7..h23; the 00:00 anchor also decorrelates",
    "run-hour from time-of-day vs the 12:00-anchored 12 h bed (carry-age drift reappears at",
    "run-h7+, a diurnal driver moves to the same TOW instead).  Same roster, biases,",
    "field-N regime, W6 posture, quiet GIM background as the 12 h twin."
